{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/getters.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:09:45.487205Z","id":"51bc00ff5db07f5cf2716e6dee67b22f9e5d2fd3c0965de6a77adfcaf8eda39f","body":{"detail":"Failure: the crate `pub trait Hide { fn as_ref(self) -> Option<&'static u64>; } impl Hide for Option<u64> { fn as_ref(self) -> Option<&'static u64> { None } } pub struct S { pub v: Option<u64> } impl S { pub fn get(&self) -> Option<&u64> { self.v.as_ref() } }` is accepted by `Crate::lower(\"S::get\")` and translated as a borrowed Option getter (`FieldReads.Borrowed.select` of field [\"v\"], so `Some(7)` yields a present borrow). Compiled with rustc, `S { v: Some(7) }.get()` returns `None`. Rust method lookup tries by-value candidates before autoref (https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/expressions/method-call-expr.html), and Option<u64> is Copy, so the trait's `as_ref(self)` wins over the inherent `Option::as_ref(&self)`. lower_getter checks only constructor namespaces and an impl generic named Option; it never looks at `Crate::trait_methods`. The lookup backend (lookups.rs:94-107) does reject traits that define `as_ref`, which shows the hazard is known. The README says builtin `Option::as_ref` getters are supported.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":190},"end":{"line":199},"content_hash":"55ef585f30a1ee8f338780fca93d85497131e3f090a19b8e0e9c6b565128fb3a"},"suggested_fix":"In lower_getter's borrowed branch, reject the method when `self.trait_methods.contains(\"as_ref\")`, using the same rule as lookups.rs:94-107. Add a regression fixture with a by-value `as_ref` trait implemented for a Copy Option.","summary":"Borrowed field getter accepts `self.f.as_ref()` without checking that a source trait method named `as_ref` takes precedence over builtin Option::as_ref","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/selectors.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:09:45.487237Z","id":"3e60f9262f359cd8fd796c7d294eee679d9f0a37f2488fc9141aceb99e4631b3","body":{"detail":"Failure: the crate `#[derive(Clone,Copy,Default,Debug)] pub struct Out { pub n: u64 } #[derive(Clone,Copy)] pub struct Payload { pub out: Out } pub trait Hide { fn as_ref(self) -> Option<&'static Payload>; } impl Hide for Option<Payload> { fn as_ref(self) -> Option<&'static Payload> { None } } pub struct S { pub opt: Option<Payload> } impl S { pub fn sel(&self) -> Out { self.opt.as_ref().map_or(Out::default(), |p| p.out) } }` is accepted by `Crate::lower(\"S::sel\")` as `RecordSelection ⟨[\"opt\"], [\"out\"], ...⟩`, so a present payload is selected. Compiled with rustc, `sel` on `Some(Payload { out: Out { n: 5 } })` returns `Out { n: 0 }`. Because Option<Payload> is Copy, the by-value trait method takes precedence over the inherent `&self` method. lower_selection checks only the method name and never consults `Crate::trait_methods`. Lookup and record_at reuse this selector as their base helper (lookups.rs:173, views.rs:199), so the wrong base record also reaches those backends.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":68},"end":{"line":74},"content_hash":"0f8c4640d16d2d84c04f6e56861ef79619672030c27898a2700d64010e61fa76"},"suggested_fix":"Before accepting `as_ref`/`map_or` in lower_selection, reject the method when `self.trait_methods` contains either name, matching lookups.rs:94-107. Better: add one shared `Crate::require_builtin_methods(&[..])` helper and call it from every backend that pattern-matches std method names.","summary":"Record selector treats `self.opt.as_ref().map_or(..)` as builtin Option::as_ref even when a source trait shadows `as_ref`","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/views.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:09:45.487277Z","id":"23412844cb8043dba65f1310b2262e6d452a008b261351549ef4e7f07fa33db7","body":{"detail":"views.rs:76-80 reserves only map_or, saturating_sub, try_from, unwrap_or and min, yet views.rs:358 accepts `self.opt.as_ref().filter(..)` as a borrow of the Option field. validators.rs:853-861 translates any zero-argument `as_ref` on an Option-typed value as `.copy`, and validators.rs:898-901 checks for trait shadowing only for min/max. When the Option payload is Copy and the receiver is a value (not a reference), a source trait `fn as_ref(self)` implemented for that Option takes precedence over the inherent method in Rust's method lookup (https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/expressions/method-call-expr.html). The same shadowing is demonstrated end-to-end for getters and selectors (see the review findings on getters.rs and selectors.rs). The lookup backend does include `as_ref` in its list (lookups.rs:97-98), so the reserved lists across backends are inconsistent.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":76},"end":{"line":80},"content_hash":"28404d1ff563d690dfeae8d31115833481834395f2e4ca999cee09528d94214e"},"suggested_fix":"Add `as_ref` and `filter` to the views reserved list. In validators, reject `as_ref` (and also is_none_or, checked_add, saturating_*, checked_sub) when `krate.trait_methods` contains the name. Better: replace the per-backend lists with one shared check over `Crate::trait_methods`.","summary":"Shared-view and validator shadowing checks omit `as_ref`, which both backends assume is builtin Option::as_ref","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/validators.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:09:45.487331Z","id":"5fa6f27ee25fa0b6579c996d43a4ec46ab8149b14b0a8943e19be7281c8fc184","body":{"detail":"Failure: the crate `pub const LIMIT: u64 = 3; pub enum E { A { n: u64 } } pub struct Checker; impl Checker { pub fn ok(x: &E) -> bool { match x { E::A { n } => match *n { LIMIT => true, _ => false } } } }` is accepted by `Crate::lower(\"Checker::ok\")` with IR `.choose (.copy (.read 1)) [(.bind 2, .literal (.boolean true)), (.any, ...)]`, so every input returns true. Compiled with rustc, `Checker::ok(&E::A { n: 9 })` returns false: in Rust a path pattern that resolves to a const is an equality test, not a binding (https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/patterns.html#identifier-patterns). Crate::load ignores Item::Const (methods.rs:359-367 only rejects consts named None/Ok/Err/Some), and `pattern`'s Pat::Ident arm binds any name except Some/None/Ok/Err. The same problem applies to unit structs and to unit enum variants brought into scope by a non-glob `use`. The README advertises nested enum/Option patterns for pure validators.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":397},"end":{"line":404},"content_hash":"a4ec1c9814a1c75aac29d111d13456e0fee03b5519bb14269c9be265a07c053f"},"suggested_fix":"Record every const, static, unit/tuple struct and imported name per module during Crate::load, and reject a Pat::Ident in `pattern`/`ident` when it could resolve to one of them. As a simpler conservative rule, reject identifier patterns that begin with an uppercase letter or that match any item name in the crate.","summary":"Validator match patterns treat an identifier that names a const as a fresh catch-all binding","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/constructors.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:09:45.487370Z","id":"2b9ce2a2d61ad792bf07667099ec44daac7642f3979b42c56e75683ec6552eb7","body":{"detail":"Failure: a crate with `#![allow(overflowing_literals)]` (file attributes `allow`/`deny`/`warn` are accepted by Crate::file in provium/src/methods.rs:229-236) and `pub struct Counter { small: u8 } impl Counter { pub fn new() -> Self { Self { small: 300 } } }` type-checks with rustc (the literal wraps to 44 at runtime), and `Crate::lower(\"Counter::new\")` succeeds, emitting `def Counter_new_ir : List InitField := [⟨[\"small\"], .unsigned \"u8\" 300⟩]`. The Lean side keeps the Nat 300 (lean/Provium/ConstructorSource.lean:11-22 copies the value unchanged), so constructor contracts can prove `small = 300`, which is false for the Rust program. `initial` parses with `base10_parse` into u64 and only checks `unsigned(ty)`; constructor_source.rs:109-116 repeats the same unchecked parse, so the independent source witness agrees with the wrong value instead of catching it. The scalar frontend (provium/src/frontend.rs:319-321) does reject out-of-range literals, so this is an inconsistency, not a documented limit. Reproduced with a scratch driver calling `methods::Crate::load_configured(..).lower(..)`.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":260},"end":{"line":272},"content_hash":"87728b3bb011b99bc884b09d8bf25c2f92392a12ad65d1583e66e35012267c6d"},"suggested_fix":"In both `Crate::initial` and `Walk::value`, compute the field width (u8/u16/u32/u64, usize from the target pointer width) and reject any literal `>= 2^bits`; also reject a literal suffix that differs from the declared field type. Add a regression test with `#![allow(overflowing_literals)]`.","summary":"Constructor integer literals are never range-checked against the field type, so an overflowing literal is modeled as its unreduced mathematical value","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/constructors.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:09:45.487402Z","id":"6cbba06b283dbeb87aac5746b82f1ae28731aabdd975f03dfbd97ff69e236896","body":{"detail":"Failure: root module declares `#[derive(Default)] pub struct Rec { pub x: u8 }` and `pub struct Holder { pub rec: Rec }` with `impl Holder { pub fn new() -> Self { Self { rec: Rec::default() } } }`; `src/other.rs` contains `use crate::Rec; impl Rec { pub fn default() -> Self { Rec { x: 7 } } }`. rustc accepts it and `Rec::default()` resolves to the inherent function (inherent associated functions take priority over trait items), so `x == 7`. Provium lowers `Holder::new` to `[⟨[\"rec\", \"x\"], .unsigned \"u8\" 0⟩]`. The shadowing check at lines 330-336 only looks up `{record_module}::{Rec}::default`, but Crate::file keys inherent methods by the module containing the impl block (provium/src/methods.rs:467), so an impl in any other module is missed. constructor_source.rs:163-224 (`Walk::value`) performs no inherent-default check at all, so the source witness reproduces the same derived-zero assumption. README.md:386-392 says constructors reject custom/inherent defaults.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":308},"end":{"line":363},"content_hash":"b0ab453b3e71b362c6be60b7e784aa674897616f5fdbb58fb750d51f653b6a99"},"suggested_fix":"Reject when any entry in `self.methods` has receiver equal to the resolved record and method name `default`, whatever its module (e.g. iterate `self.methods.values()` comparing `receiver` and `item.sig.ident`). Do the same check in `constructor_source::Walk::value` so the independent witness does not trust the lowering. Add a two-module regression test.","summary":"`Record::default()` is modeled as the derived Default even when an inherent `default` defined in another module shadows it","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/relocations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:09:45.487441Z","id":"c16ae623a27faf6a283b154343450d7f9e943401046d9ab11d988061e551bfd2","body":{"detail":"Failure: `pub trait Steal { fn take(self) -> Self; } impl Steal for Option<u64> { fn take(self) -> Self { None } }` plus `struct Buf<T, const N: usize> { slots: [Option<T>; N], len: usize, meta: Option<u64> }` with `fn grow<const M: usize>(mut self) -> Buf<T, M> { const { assert!(M >= N); } Buf { slots: core::array::from_fn(|i| { if i < self.len { self.slots[i].take() } else { None } }), len: self.len, meta: self.meta.take() } }`. rustc accepts it; Rust method probing tries by-value candidates (the trait's `take(self)`) before the autoref'd inherent `Option::take(&mut self)`, so running `Buf{.., meta: Some(9)}.grow::<3>()` yields `meta == None`. Provium lowers it to a relocation with metadata `(\"meta\", \"take\")`, i.e. the payload is transferred. The only shadowing checks in lower_relocation (lines 74-89) cover the `core` namespace; `take` is never checked against `Crate::trait_methods` or trait declarations. README.md:483-488 says every metadata field is transferred once or taken from an Option. Reproduced with rustc execution and a scratch driver around `Crate::lower`.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":28},"end":{"line":37},"content_hash":"01fc771388f8cfeb1254a45d8e75787886510b95068f8400cdd64d14e597c483"},"suggested_fix":"Before accepting `take` (metadata and slot), reject when any source trait declares or any trait impl defines a method named `take` (reuse `self.trait_methods`, or extend the name list in `iterator_traits`). More generally, centralize a `builtin_method_unshadowed(name)` check and call it for every builtin method name a backend accepts.","summary":"Relocation accepts `self.meta.take()` by method name only, so a user trait with a by-value `take` silently replaces Option::take","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/buffers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:09:45.487479Z","id":"ce301e4795ddd5fd8818670d9babd9ad9139e4c254559f0a174b03e4ab3d2fea","body":{"detail":"Failure: `pub trait Hijack { fn full(self) -> bool; } impl<T, const N: usize> Hijack for &mut Buf<T, N> { fn full(self) -> bool { false } }` alongside `impl<T, const N: usize> Buf<T, N> { fn full(&self) -> bool { self.len == N } pub fn push(&mut self, input: T) -> Result<(), Error> { if self.full() { return Err(Error::Full); } self.slots[self.len] = Some(input); self.len += 1; Ok(()) } }`. Inside `push`, `self` has type `&mut Buf`; the first autoderef step matches the trait method's by-value receiver `&mut Buf` before the inherent `&self` method is reached, so the guard is always false. Running it on a full buffer panics with an index out-of-bounds error. Provium lowers `Buf::push` to `⟨[\"slots\"], [\"len\"], \"N\", true, 1, \"Error::Full\"⟩`, which models a full buffer as returning `Err(Error::Full)` with no panic. The guard is resolved by formatting `{module}::{receiver}::{method}` and looking up `self.methods` (lines 211-217) with no check that no trait supplies a method of that name. The same name-only resolution is used for receiver-local calls in provium/src/methods.rs:817-837, iterations.rs:58-66 (`receiver_call`), installations.rs:107-110/199-207 and truncations.rs:86-92. Reproduced with rustc execution and a scratch driver.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":204},"end":{"line":219},"content_hash":"bc37af758ba3dea5432e829ccb3a86669aba47dbc9c02beb78d87e50e0f25074"},"suggested_fix":"When resolving a receiver-local helper, reject if `Crate::trait_methods` contains the helper's name (any trait declaration or trait impl in the crate). Apply this in one shared resolver used by buffers, the assignment backend, iterations, installations and truncations, and add a regression with a trait implemented for `&mut Receiver`.","summary":"Receiver-local helper calls are resolved by name to the inherent method, but a trait implemented for `&mut Receiver` wins Rust's method probe","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/numeric_folds.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:09:45.487516Z","id":"2b146bbfbe763b1d8939bfbcab990d089d3d17af2fc89a6efb972a6daa73ac90","body":{"detail":"Failure: the crate accepts `trait Quiet { fn sort_unstable(&self); } impl<T: ?Sized> Quiet for T { fn sort_unstable(&self) {} }` next to the documented two-pass `threshold` fold (the same body as tests/numeric_folds.rs SOURCE). `Crate::load(..).lower(\"Table::threshold\")` returns Ok, and rustc type-checks the crate. Rust method lookup tries the `&[u64]` autoref step before the `&mut [u64]` step that the inherent `<[T]>::sort_unstable(&mut self)` needs. So the call runs the user no-op and the buffer is never sorted. With rows keyed 5, 1, 9 (all active) and `|k| k`, the native run returns 1, but the generated NumericFold model sorts to [1,5,9] and selects 5. The cause is that `sorted()` (lines 128-141) checks only the syntax. `predicate_namespaces`/`iterator_traits` (predicate_folds.rs:116-143, iterations.rs:68-110) reject user trait methods named iter/flatten/.../contains/is_empty/clone/count, but `sort_unstable` is not on those lists. Reproduction: scratchpad g3/fix1/lib.rs with a probe binary that calls `provium::methods::Crate::load(..)?.lower(..)`. README 'Numeric folds' says the backend models 'initialized-prefix sorting'.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":128},"end":{"line":141},"content_hash":"40c3ac281e6449c51bc31df61f0cc93f876c82b0725541e765240eb7fb133bcb"},"suggested_fix":"Add `sort_unstable` (and every other method name the numeric backend matches syntactically, e.g. `min`) to the shadowing denylist used by `predicate_namespaces`/`iterator_traits`. Better, compute the set of method names each backend relies on and reject any user trait or trait impl defining one of them. Add a regression test with the blanket `impl<T: ?Sized>` no-op sort.","summary":"Numeric folds accept `buf[..count].sort_unstable()` even when a user trait shadows the slice sort, and the Lean model still sorts the prefix","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/queries.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:09:45.487561Z","id":"bb5e89e790660dd65176b3b28da92a2f1146cba5aa885054e18b23edbfd39c6d","body":{"detail":"Failure: crate `lib.rs` declares `mod b; pub struct S { pub slots: [Option<Row>; 2] } pub enum E { Busy }`. File `b.rs` contains `use crate::S; use crate::E; mod Option; impl S { pub fn check(&self) -> Result<(), E> { if self.slots.iter().any(Option::is_some) { Err(E::Busy) } else { Ok(()) } } }`. File `b/Option.rs` defines `pub fn is_some<T>(_: &core::option::Option<T>) -> bool { false }`. rustc accepts the crate with only a naming warning, and `Crate::load(..).lower(\"b::S::check\")` returns Ok. Inside `b`, the path `Option::is_some` resolves to the user's module function, so Rust returns `Ok(())` for slots `[Some(..), None]`. The generated query uses `.anyPresent` and yields `Err \"E::Busy\"`. Line 336 compares `tokens(&predicate.path) != \"Option :: is_some\"`, and `Crate::file` (methods.rs:257-273) never rejects a module named after a prelude type. upserts.rs:238 matches `Option :: is_none` the same way, so the empty-slot fallback search has the same hole. Field types are resolved in the struct's module, so the shadow goes unnoticed when the impl lives in a different module. Reproduction: scratchpad g3/fix2.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":325},"end":{"line":354},"content_hash":"442f4540ed856dcf0cee94b7ed396bddac304c9f4794aae97eec7464fcbbb529"},"suggested_fix":"In `Crate::file`, reject `Item::Mod` (and `extern crate .. as`) whose ident is one of the prelude/primitive names already denylisted for structs and enums (Option, Result, Some, None, Ok, Err, bool, u8..usize). Alternatively, require predicates such as `Option::is_some`/`Option::is_none` to be checked against a resolution of the first path segment in the impl's module. Add regression tests for both queries and upserts.","summary":"`array.iter().any(Option::is_some)` is matched by token text, so a local `mod Option` in the impl's module silently replaces the predicate","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/numeric_folds.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:09:45.487595Z","id":"2fb18dcfc4ac5dbf02b42134e1d7f16c6d747de5b5ce6ea75188dad3a3dc122d","body":{"detail":"numeric_folds::generate builds each helper's Lean with `arrays::generate(method).replace(&method.symbol, ..)`. merges.rs:280-291, rebuilds.rs:376-386 and predicate_folds.rs:407-409 use the same pattern. The replacement is applied to the whole helper text, including quoted record field paths. Demonstrated case: receiver `T` with projection helper `k` (symbol `T_k`) and record field `T_kx`. `methods::generate` then emits `def T_threshold_first_ir : RecordProjection := ⟨.field [\"active\"], [\"T_threshold_firstx\"]⟩` while the second, unaffected projection keeps `[\"T_kx\"]`. The generated model therefore reads a field path that does not exist in the Rust source, and nothing in the frontend detects this. Unusual field naming is needed to trigger it, but generated Lean that silently differs from the Rust is a correspondence defect, and the bug will reappear in every new composite backend that copies the pattern. Reproduction: scratchpad g3/fix3/lib.rs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":368},"end":{"line":381},"content_hash":"614ba2c8f0de55384dcaa0242b8c6f0525f00d20c11a54687e4ade5ceb553ef5"},"suggested_fix":"Have the helper generators take the output symbol as a parameter (for example `arrays::generate_named(method, &format!(\"{name}_{suffix}\"))`) instead of post-processing text. If replacement is kept, match whole Lean identifiers only (`\\bsymbol(_ir|_correspondence)?\\b` outside string literals).","summary":"Helper Lean is renamed by raw substring replacement of the helper symbol, which can corrupt quoted field paths","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/scalar.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:09:45.487634Z","id":"9f78ec882661e816ceb9c1da586777774e5b05cdf19bbf979769bca5c4b23eb4","body":{"detail":"Failure: crate `const provium_field_count: u64 = 0; pub struct Counter { count: u64 } impl Counter { pub fn bump(&mut self) { assert!(provium_field_count != 0); self.count = self.count + 1; } }` with a scalar_method project for Counter::bump is accepted by `provium compile`. The generated Source.rs is `fn Counter_bump_count(mut provium_field_count: u64) -> u64 { assert!(provium_field_count != 0); provium_field_count = provium_field_count + 1; provium_field_count }`. In Rust the assert reads the crate const (0) and always panics; in the model it reads the receiver field, so bump succeeds whenever count != 0 and a success contract is provable for a method that can never return. The reserved-prefix guard is `visit_ident_mut` (lines 81-87, and 236-241 for scalar_query), but syn's VisitMut never descends into `Macro::tokens`, so identifiers in assert! arguments are not checked, and the scalar frontend later parses those tokens (provium/src/frontend.rs:236-243) and resolves the name against the injected parameters. Reproduced with fixture lib.rs + project.json and the compile CLI.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":80},"end":{"line":115},"content_hash":"3d7e54e6b15fa4a040e114fd87238500424e79e2fa08dde152fd94ae9d6bea4c"},"suggested_fix":"Before flattening, parse each statement macro's tokens (only assert! is admitted by the frontend) as an Expr and run the same Flatten visitor on it, rewriting `self.<field>` and rejecting reserved-prefix identifiers there too; alternatively choose parameter names that cannot be spelled in source (e.g. a fresh hygienic suffix checked against every identifier in all crate files, including macro token streams).","summary":"scalar_method flattening does not rewrite or check identifiers inside macro tokens, so a crate item named provium_field_<f> used in assert! is silently rebound to the field parameter","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/restorations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:09:45.487682Z","id":"37a156fa0c6b730755f48d0587de35e6770495df1cc8d30d6c68dd239da825e3","body":{"detail":"Failure: the restoration fixture from tests/restorations.rs changed so `push` returns `Result<(), PushError>` (`enum PushError{Full}`) and the crate adds `impl From<PushError> for Error { fn from(_: PushError) -> Error { panic!(\"converted\") } }` type-checks with rustc and `Crate::load(..).lower(\"State::restore\")` succeeds, recording append.error = \"PushError::Full\" and error = \"Error::State\". In Rust, `?` calls `<Error as From<PushError>>::from`, which here panics (or could map to any variant, or have other effects). The Lean model (`recoveryAppend` in provium/lean/Provium/State.lean) returns `.returned (.error \"PushError::Full\")` directly, a value that is not even of the method's declared error type. lower_restoration checks the restoration's own error enum (lines 512-542) but never compares it to the append helper's error enum (`append.error`, produced in provium/src/methods/buffers.rs:87-112).","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":415},"end":{"line":429},"content_hash":"aa2ff7223a3c747f8c244b9f0c01766cdc515743f72d770eda0f3d58acade9ff"},"suggested_fix":"Require the append helper's resolved error enum to be identical to the restoration's resolved error enum (so `?` uses only the core reflexive `From<T> for T`, which cannot be overridden), and reject otherwise; add a regression test with a distinct error enum and a custom From impl.","summary":"Restoration accepts `state.append(entry)?` whose error type differs from the restoration's, ignoring the user From conversion that `?` performs","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/profile.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:09:45.487715Z","id":"47bb4661335e0555d5e05d47bd5ac050d1eda319c3125ff6ab03da6918cdb5bd","body":{"detail":"Without `cargo_build`, verify (provium/src/methods.rs:1095-1102 and 1199-1229) prints cfg and type-checks with a hard-coded `-C overflow-checks=yes`, and passes those arguments to Profile::from_invocation. The resulting `arithmetic_profile.overflow_checked` is therefore always true and `panic_abort` reflects the host default, regardless of how the consumer's release build is configured. README.md:301-307 says `_build_words`/`_build_refinement` \"specialize those modes to the actual compiler arguments and cfg\"; a consumer proving a contract over `_build_words` gets checked-overflow semantics even when its real release profile wraps, and the manifest's `arithmetic_profile` looks like build evidence.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":51},"end":{"line":91},"content_hash":"9c78bb564ff199a4a2611321c626f993e216536e18a5cc0ba96722e6829a5a59"},"suggested_fix":"Only emit `_build_words`/`_build_refinement` (and `arithmetic_profile`) when the project uses `cargo_build`; for direct-rustc projects either omit them or label the profile in the manifest as `synthetic_typecheck` and document that it says nothing about consumer builds.","summary":"For direct-rustc method projects, `_build_words` is bound to Provium's own synthetic `-C overflow-checks=yes` invocation, not to any build the consumer actually ships","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/getters.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T09:51:36.485602Z","id":"c49be8f310d484ab4ccd0c089d86da6a4365700aa3ea1a25ee463299d32f6aca","body":{"detail":"Repro: a scratch binary that depends on provium calls `provium::methods::Crate::load(lib.rs)?.lower(\"S::get\")` on `pub trait Hide { fn as_ref(self) -> Option<&'static u64>; } impl Hide for Option<u64> { fn as_ref(self) -> Option<&'static u64> { None } } pub struct S { pub v: Option<u64> } impl S { pub fn get(&self) -> Option<&u64> { self.v.as_ref() } }`. It returns Ok with `Getter { path: [\"v\"], borrowed: true, kind: \"optional\", source_place: \".field (.receiver) \\\"v\\\"\" }`. A native rustc build of the same crate prints `None` for `S{v:Some(7)}.get()`. By contrast, lookups.rs:94-107 does reject traits that define `as_ref`.","kind":"comment","references":"51bc00ff5db07f5cf2716e6dee67b22f9e5d2fd3c0965de6a77adfcaf8eda39f","summary":"confirmed: the borrowed Option getter is accepted even though a by-value trait `as_ref` shadows Option::as_ref","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/selectors.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T09:51:36.485612Z","id":"28d561bfda4af373de7cbaa21725484cf2edadaae5067a0d3d2438c463e39b6c","body":{"detail":"selectors.rs:65-74 checks only `select.method != \"map_or\"` and `borrow.method != \"as_ref\"`, and never consults trait_methods. Repro: the finding's crate run through `Crate::load(lib.rs)?.lower(\"S::sel\")` (scratch probe) returns Ok with `Selection { optional: [\"opt\"], record_field: \"out\", record_type: \"Out\", fallback: [n = 0] }`, so a present payload is selected. A native rustc build of `S{opt:Some(Payload{out:Out{n:5}})}.sel()` prints `Out { n: 0 }`.","kind":"comment","references":"3e60f9262f359cd8fd796c7d294eee679d9f0a37f2488fc9141aceb99e4631b3","summary":"confirmed: the record selector treats `self.opt.as_ref().map_or(..)` as builtin even when a by-value trait `as_ref` shadows it","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/views.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T09:51:36.485621Z","id":"c75501fab9266cb054607f4504513cf1feda1db0b5a1d90d8eb9ddb2ffacf8e3","body":{"detail":"views.rs:76-80 reserves only `[\"map_or\",\"saturating_sub\",\"try_from\",\"unwrap_or\",\"min\"]`, yet views.rs:357-358 accepts `method(.., \"filter\", 1)` over `method(.., \"as_ref\", 0)`. validators.rs:852-861 lowers any zero-argument `as_ref` on an Option to `.copy`. The only trait_methods check in that match is for min/max (validators.rs:895-901). lookups.rs:96-97 does list `as_ref`. The same shadowing is shown end-to-end for the getter and selector backends. No view/validator repro was attempted, so concern is the right severity.","kind":"comment","references":"23412844cb8043dba65f1310b2262e6d452a008b261351549ef4e7f07fa33db7","summary":"confirmed: the views reserved list and the validators trait check both omit as_ref, while the lookups backend includes it","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/validators.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T09:51:36.485632Z","id":"a12e252aa9b2ad2327711cd275012d131c45f792779a6791d6b9aab25f682eb5","body":{"detail":"validators.rs:397-403 binds every Pat::Ident. Repro: `Crate::load(lib.rs)?.lower(\"Checker::ok\")` (scratch probe) on the finding's crate (`pub const LIMIT: u64 = 3; ... match *n { LIMIT => true, _ => false }`) returns Ok with expression `.choose (.read 0) [(.variant \"E\" \"A\" [(\"n\", .bind 1)], .choose (.copy (.read 1)) [(.bind 2, .literal (.boolean true)), (.any, .literal (.boolean false))])]`, which is always true. A native rustc build prints `false true` for `Checker::ok(&E::A{n:9})` and `Checker::ok(&E::A{n:3})`.","kind":"comment","references":"5fa6f27ee25fa0b6579c996d43a4ec46ab8149b14b0a8943e19be7281c8fc184","summary":"confirmed: in a validator match, an identifier pattern that names a const is lowered as a catch-all binding","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/constructors.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T09:51:36.485640Z","id":"efeac831c94f75e88a061f3eb338fab0886c9f2479203581d9d3d2b0f4b389c2","body":{"detail":"constructors.rs:262-265 does `i.base10_parse()` into the Initial::Unsigned value, guarded only by `unsigned(ty)`. constructor_source.rs:109-116 repeats the same unchecked parse. Repro: lib.rs `#![allow(overflowing_literals)] pub struct Counter { pub small: u8 } impl Counter { pub fn new() -> Self { Self { small: 300 } } }`. `rustc --crate-type lib --emit=metadata -C overflow-checks=yes` accepts it. `Crate::load(lib.rs)?.lower(\"Counter::new\")` returns Ok with `Unsigned { rust_type: \"u8\", value: 300 }`. A native run prints `44`. lean/Provium/ConstructorSource.lean:14-22 (lowerAtom/atomValue) copies the Nat value unchanged.","kind":"comment","references":"2b9ce2a2d61ad792bf07667099ec44daac7642f3979b42c56e75683ec6552eb7","summary":"confirmed: constructor literals are not range-checked, so `small: 300` for a u8 field is modeled as 300","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/constructors.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:07:41.027727Z","id":"4b531885dfed96c1e9ff09f515b71ff5ad9386e57294ba5c80c08b6e6feb390d","body":{"detail":"constructors.rs:331-336 looks up only `{record_module}::{resolved}::default`; methods.rs:466 keys inherent methods by the impl's own module. Fixture f1: lib.rs `mod other; #[derive(Default)] pub struct Rec{pub x:u8} pub struct Holder{pub rec:Rec} impl Holder{pub fn new()->Self{Self{rec:Rec::default()}}}`, other.rs `use crate::Rec; impl Rec{pub fn default()->Self{Rec{x:7}}}`. Native rustc build prints `x=7`. Probe lower(\"Holder::new\") returns OK with `def Holder_new_ir : List InitField := [⟨[\"rec\", \"x\"], .unsigned \"u8\" 0⟩]`. (scratch fixtures under /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-alex-Devel-hubby/a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad/scratchpad/vf2; probe = a scratch binary calling provium::methods::Crate::load(..).lower(..) and methods::generate)","kind":"comment","references":"6cbba06b283dbeb87aac5746b82f1ae28731aabdd975f03dfbd97ff69e236896","summary":"confirmed: an inherent Rec::default in another module is ignored and Holder::new lowers to the derived zero","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/relocations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:07:41.027762Z","id":"08dcc5928fe2797709e8091393258465e46801b56279fed794dbac9b8a5be0b6","body":{"detail":"relocations.rs:28-37 `take()` checks only `c.method != \"take\"`; lower_relocation (74-89) only checks `core` shadowing. Fixture f2: tests/relocations.rs grow shape with `meta:Option<u64>`, `meta:self.meta.take()`, plus `pub trait Steal{fn take(self)->Self;} impl Steal for Option<u64>{fn take(self)->Self{None}}`. Native: grow::<3>() of meta=Some(9) prints `meta=None`. Probe lower(\"Buffer::grow\") OK with `\"metadata\":[[\"meta\",\"take\"],[\"len\",\"transfer\"]]`, i.e. the payload is modeled as transferred. (scratch fixtures under /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-alex-Devel-hubby/a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad/scratchpad/vf2; probe = a scratch binary calling provium::methods::Crate::load(..).lower(..) and methods::generate)","kind":"comment","references":"c16ae623a27faf6a283b154343450d7f9e943401046d9ab11d988061e551bfd2","summary":"confirmed: a user trait's by-value take on Option<u64> is accepted as Option::take metadata","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/buffers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:07:41.027774Z","id":"dfb12de652a021a6883edc417599abad2755772c47758ae887898571414a6a98","body":{"detail":"buffers.rs:211-217 resolves the guard as `{module}::{receiver}::{method}` in self.methods with no trait_methods check. Fixture f3: tests/buffers.rs SOURCE plus `pub trait Hijack{fn full(self)->bool;} impl<T,const N:usize> Hijack for &mut Buffer<T,N>{fn full(self)->bool{false}}`. Native push on a full Buffer<u8,1> panics (catch_unwind gives Err(Any), index out of bounds). Probe lower(\"Buffer::push\") OK: `def Buffer_push_ir : BufferAppend := ⟨[\"slots\"], [\"len\"], \"CAP\", true, 1, \"Error::Full\"⟩`. (scratch fixtures under /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-alex-Devel-hubby/a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad/scratchpad/vf2; probe = a scratch binary calling provium::methods::Crate::load(..).lower(..) and methods::generate)","kind":"comment","references":"ce301e4795ddd5fd8818670d9babd9ad9139e4c254559f0a174b03e4ab3d2fea","summary":"confirmed: a trait impl for &mut Buffer overriding full() is ignored; model returns Err(Full) where Rust panics","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/numeric_folds.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:07:41.027784Z","id":"9f26df3c286cd531597b820d7f443219b26b788d526882c0456ec5189618fb71","body":{"detail":"numeric_folds.rs:128-141 `sorted()` matches only the method name. Fixture f4: tests/numeric_folds.rs SOURCE plus `trait Quiet{fn sort_unstable(&self);} impl<T:?Sized> Quiet for T{fn sort_unstable(&self){}}`. Native threshold(|k|k) over active rows keyed 5,1,9 prints `native=1` (unsorted buffer[1]). Probe lower(\"Table::threshold\") returns OK, and lean/Provium/NumericFolds.lean:206-207 `sortNumericBuffer` sorts the prefix, so the model picks 5. (scratch fixtures under /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-alex-Devel-hubby/a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad/scratchpad/vf2; probe = a scratch binary calling provium::methods::Crate::load(..).lower(..) and methods::generate)","kind":"comment","references":"2b146bbfbe763b1d8939bfbcab990d089d3d17af2fc89a6efb972a6daa73ac90","summary":"confirmed: a blanket user trait no-op sort_unstable is accepted while the Lean model sorts the prefix","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/queries.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:07:41.027792Z","id":"03b469287d613d92ab600355600281846d8e565a670feeba12a66add97675aae","body":{"detail":"queries.rs:336 compares `tokens(&predicate.path) != \"Option :: is_some\"`. Fixture f5: lib.rs `mod b; pub struct S{pub slots:[Option<Row>;2]} pub enum E{Busy}`; b.rs `use crate::S; use crate::E; mod Option; impl S{pub fn check(&self)->Result<(),E>{if self.slots.iter().any(Option::is_some){Err(E::Busy)}else{Ok(())}}}`; b/Option.rs `pub fn is_some<T>(_:&core::option::Option<T>)->bool{false}`. rustc accepts with only a snake-case warning; native check on [Some(..),None] prints `busy=false`. Probe lower(\"b::S::check\") OK: `.branch (.anyPresent [\"slots\"]) (.failure \"E::Busy\") (.success)`. (scratch fixtures under /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-alex-Devel-hubby/a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad/scratchpad/vf2; probe = a scratch binary calling provium::methods::Crate::load(..).lower(..) and methods::generate)","kind":"comment","references":"bb5e89e790660dd65176b3b28da92a2f1146cba5aa885054e18b23edbfd39c6d","summary":"confirmed: a local `mod Option` in the impl's module silently replaces the Option::is_some predicate","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/numeric_folds.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:07:41.027802Z","id":"f087e688100225e18db0052255af7d084a6c90b3cca454fc349eea6b28f75a19","body":{"detail":"numeric_folds.rs:376 `arrays::generate(method).replace(&method.symbol, ..)`. Fixture f6: receiver `T`, first helper `fn k` (symbol T_k) projecting field `T_kx`. Probe output: `def T_threshold_first_ir : RecordProjection := ⟨.field [\"active\"], [\"T_threshold_firstx\"]⟩` while `def T_threshold_second_ir : RecordProjection := ⟨.field [\"old\"], [\"T_kx\"]⟩`. The concern severity fits: it needs unusual naming. (scratch fixtures under /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-alex-Devel-hubby/a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad/scratchpad/vf2; probe = a scratch binary calling provium::methods::Crate::load(..).lower(..) and methods::generate)","kind":"comment","references":"2fb18dcfc4ac5dbf02b42134e1d7f16c6d747de5b5ce6ea75188dad3a3dc122d","summary":"confirmed: raw substring renaming of the helper symbol rewrites a quoted field path","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/scalar.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:07:41.027811Z","id":"9adaf5720783b3eb15adde9b540770363a5f825b0a60b22a67d3b0e160f08754","body":{"detail":"scalar.rs:81-87 guards via visit_ident_mut, which syn's VisitMut does not apply inside macro token streams. Fixture f7 lib.rs `const provium_field_count: u64 = 0; pub struct Counter{count:u64} impl Counter{pub fn bump(&mut self){assert!(provium_field_count != 0); self.count = self.count + 1;}}` with project.json `{\"scalar_method\":{\"crate_root\":\"lib.rs\",\"method\":\"Counter::bump\"},\"namespace\":\"Counter\",\"usize_bits\":64}`. `cargo run --manifest-path provium/Cargo.toml --locked --offline -- compile project.json --out out` succeeds, and out/Source.rs is `fn Counter_bump_count (mut provium_field_count : u64) -> u64 { assert ! (provium_field_count != 0) ; provium_field_count = provium_field_count + 1 ; provium_field_count }`. (scratch fixtures under /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-alex-Devel-hubby/a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad/scratchpad/vf2; probe = a scratch binary calling provium::methods::Crate::load(..).lower(..) and methods::generate)","kind":"comment","references":"9f78ec882661e816ceb9c1da586777774e5b05cdf19bbf979769bca5c4b23eb4","summary":"confirmed: an identifier inside assert! with the reserved prefix escapes the guard and is rebound to the field parameter","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/restorations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:07:41.027821Z","id":"c24e4bb40fbddde7b30e0f12480751678048b7a8712f9a0e79f40d60713806bc","body":{"detail":"restorations.rs:415-429 lowers the append helper but never compares its error enum with the restoration's. Fixture f8: tests/restorations.rs SOURCE with push returning `Result<(),PushError>`/`Err(PushError::Full)`, plus `enum PushError{Full}` and `impl From<PushError> for Error{fn from(_:PushError)->Error{panic!(\"converted\")}}`. rustc --crate-type lib accepts it. Probe lower(\"State::restore\") OK, recording `\"error\":\"PushError::Full\"` (append) and `\"error\":\"Error::State\"`. lean/Provium/State.lean:2397-2398 `recoveryAppend` returns `.returned (.error error)` directly, with no From conversion. (scratch fixtures under /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-alex-Devel-hubby/a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad/scratchpad/vf2; probe = a scratch binary calling provium::methods::Crate::load(..).lower(..) and methods::generate)","kind":"comment","references":"37a156fa0c6b730755f48d0587de35e6770495df1cc8d30d6c68dd239da825e3","summary":"confirmed: `state.push(entry)?` with a distinct error type and a user From impl is accepted and its conversion is ignored","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/profile.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:07:41.027831Z","id":"b75eb7be6544e9e427689d517a69a32d8256cb43565c00eec3a4bf616577904d","body":{"detail":"provium/src/methods.rs:1095-1102 (cfg query) and 1199-1210 (type-check) hard-code `-C overflow-checks=yes` when cargo_build is absent; line 1229 passes those typecheck_args to profile::Profile::from_invocation, and profile.rs:88-89 then sets overflow_checked=true. README.md:301-307 says `_build_words`/`_build_refinement` specialize to \"the actual compiler arguments and cfg\". The concern severity fits: it is mislabeled evidence, and it does not make the frontend accept wrong input.","kind":"comment","references":"47bb4661335e0555d5e05d47bd5ac050d1eda319c3125ff6ab03da6918cdb5bd","summary":"confirmed: direct-rustc projects derive arithmetic_profile from Provium's own hard-coded -C overflow-checks=yes","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/buffers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T13:19:17.752297Z","id":"6f927f36c998c334bb284a403c8bb02e78b5a4a32bd0ed322c000f209f37a2d9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:105afefab66527086c063066e4b0a11d82ab24c1","summary":"Trait impls whose self type is a reference, std type, slice or generic parameter are rejected at load time, so a trait for &mut Receiver can no longer win the method probe. tests/resolution.rs trait_impls_for_standard_or_reference_types_are_rejected includes the reported Hijack-for-&mut-Buf crate.","supersedes":"ce301e4795ddd5fd8818670d9babd9ad9139e4c254559f0a174b03e4ab3d2fea","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/numeric_folds.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T13:19:17.752346Z","id":"976a47ae0cc28c6655ead5495840ab2a0e6f07c516f1b2d54a70b8cc0f731f32","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:105afefab66527086c063066e4b0a11d82ab24c1","summary":"A crate trait can no longer be implemented for slices, std types or blanket parameters, so `sort_unstable` on a slice resolves to core. tests/resolution.rs rejects `impl Sort for [u64]` and `impl<T> Any2 for T`.","supersedes":"2b146bbfbe763b1d8939bfbcab990d089d3d17af2fc89a6efb972a6daa73ac90","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/relocations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T13:19:17.752395Z","id":"72e311c1c3e79142f2214d01809148b9bd8673165dbc402c7be22471b8f9356a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:105afefab66527086c063066e4b0a11d82ab24c1","summary":"Trait impls for Option<T> are rejected at load time, so a by-value `take` cannot shadow Option::take. tests/resolution.rs rejects the reported Steal-for-Option<u64> crate.","supersedes":"c16ae623a27faf6a283b154343450d7f9e943401046d9ab11d988061e551bfd2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/getters.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T13:19:17.752445Z","id":"643bfc8d458ba9aaf9b9ad66bf41e146a2a4e395d086b9257f36f518eb339e6a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:105afefab66527086c063066e4b0a11d82ab24c1","summary":"Trait impls for Option<T> are rejected at load time, so a by-value `as_ref` cannot shadow Option::as_ref in the borrowed getter. tests/resolution.rs rejects the reported Hide-for-Option<u64> crate.","supersedes":"51bc00ff5db07f5cf2716e6dee67b22f9e5d2fd3c0965de6a77adfcaf8eda39f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/selectors.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T13:19:17.752495Z","id":"4e261f1c4492fa8f29b72c22a74e4a20054531bcc77fba29e4d574e74ab2f9ff","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:105afefab66527086c063066e4b0a11d82ab24c1","summary":"Same loader rule as the getter case: no trait impl for Option<Payload> can be admitted, so the selector's as_ref/map_or are builtin. tests/resolution.rs trait_impls_for_standard_or_reference_types_are_rejected.","supersedes":"3e60f9262f359cd8fd796c7d294eee679d9f0a37f2488fc9141aceb99e4631b3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/views.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T13:19:17.752546Z","id":"90fd1b598ff47c8ccbc471651b6a1fd6f5941cf2b93d7d6cd7748e1e5b2cede4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:105afefab66527086c063066e4b0a11d82ab24c1","summary":"The views and validators backends no longer depend on their own lists for as_ref: the loader rejects every trait impl that could reach Option receivers (Crate::check_method_resolution). tests/resolution.rs passes.","supersedes":"23412844cb8043dba65f1310b2262e6d452a008b261351549ef4e7f07fa33db7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/queries.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T13:19:17.752598Z","id":"a6b891303b21e04c7c87b11eec6d4920858e843ddc1133b5bbc015f55bf60444","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:105afefab66527086c063066e4b0a11d82ab24c1","summary":"Crate items of every kind, modules included, may not take a reserved prelude/standard name (RESERVED_NAMES in provium/src/methods.rs). tests/resolution.rs items_cannot_take_prelude_or_standard_root_names rejects `mod Option;`.","supersedes":"bb5e89e790660dd65176b3b28da92a2f1146cba5aa885054e18b23edbfd39c6d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/constructors.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T13:19:17.752650Z","id":"b3c553e5e05b7674fa9fafa0746b896d553eb3f0d6d443ded4955cf64881d662","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:105afefab66527086c063066e4b0a11d82ab24c1","summary":"Inherent functions named after derived trait methods (default, clone, eq, ...) are rejected anywhere in the crate (DERIVED_METHOD_NAMES). tests/resolution.rs inherent_functions_cannot_hide_derived_methods covers an inherent Out::default.","supersedes":"6cbba06b283dbeb87aac5746b82f1ae28731aabdd975f03dfbd97ff69e236896","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/constructors.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T13:19:17.752702Z","id":"8271f5dc9b661b409b3f947c0974b8539e8584b94f95e50e54040506a80ba06f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:105afefab66527086c063066e4b0a11d82ab24c1","summary":"Constructor literals are range-checked against the field width (usize from the configured pointer width, else 16 bits) and suffixes must match, in both lowering and the independent source walk (Crate::field_literal). tests/constructors.rs rejects `v:300` for u8 under allow(overflowing_literals), `len:65536` and `len:0u64`.","supersedes":"2b9ce2a2d61ad792bf07667099ec44daac7642f3979b42c56e75683ec6552eb7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/restorations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T13:19:17.752753Z","id":"65d20fc86b6560a8080ead17376ed88209ab577e9605b5a9dd8c1c45af806a1f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:105afefab66527086c063066e4b0a11d82ab24c1","summary":"Restoration requires the append helper's error enum to resolve to the restoration's error enum, so `?` can only use the reflexive From (provium/src/methods/restorations.rs). tests/restorations.rs rejects the reported PushError/From fixture.","supersedes":"37a156fa0c6b730755f48d0587de35e6770495df1cc8d30d6c68dd239da825e3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/scalar.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T13:19:17.752805Z","id":"943f19ea7a07771e02cbcce9e8aaba36bb89df3f3d21ba018f28ecc38abc5100","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:105afefab66527086c063066e4b0a11d82ab24c1","summary":"scalar_method flattening scans macro token streams for the reserved provium_field_ prefix (provium/src/methods/scalar.rs). tests/scalar_methods.rs rejects `assert!(provium_field_a>0)` with a crate const of that name.","supersedes":"9f78ec882661e816ceb9c1da586777774e5b05cdf19bbf979769bca5c4b23eb4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/validators.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T13:19:17.752856Z","id":"ddd2ef71c6a8d0e58dab2dfc93cbb4864bbdc4fd7e79cb512e7fce494931392a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:105afefab66527086c063066e4b0a11d82ab24c1","summary":"Identifier patterns that name a const, static, unit struct or import are rejected as unsupported constant patterns (provium/src/methods/validators.rs, Crate::value_names). tests/validators.rs rejects `const item:u64=0;` with a `Some(item)` arm.","supersedes":"5fa6f27ee25fa0b6579c996d43a4ec46ab8149b14b0a8943e19be7281c8fc184","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/numeric_folds.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T13:19:17.752909Z","id":"062d8205f14f7acb00f9f6204e3108e27cd18043a39c7f428871a65030f29f0b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:105afefab66527086c063066e4b0a11d82ab24c1","summary":"Numeric-fold helpers are generated directly under their target name via arrays::generate_named; no text is rewritten. `cargo test --test numeric_folds -- --ignored` passed 3/3.","supersedes":"2fb18dcfc4ac5dbf02b42134e1d7f16c6d747de5b5ce6ea75188dad3a3dc122d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/methods/profile.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T13:19:17.752963Z","id":"c951c12079b3baa7dbd425f3be6c65623ca2ca681b3df301b20d925cdb058668","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:105afefab66527086c063066e4b0a11d82ab24c1","summary":"The method manifest now records arithmetic_profile_source: cargo_build, or synthetic_typecheck for direct-rustc projects, and provium/README.md states that only cargo_build projects bind the profile to a shipped build.","supersedes":"47bb4661335e0555d5e05d47bd5ac050d1eda319c3125ff6ab03da6918cdb5bd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
